source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A cell holding one space is a cell of its own: Jira renders the two data cells `a` and `&nbsp;`. The space stands at the cell's edge, where GFM keeps none, so jiro keeps the rows raw.
-- input.jira --
||h||i||
|a| |
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>i</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h||i||
|a| |
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
